Z||000006||Formula88||08-07-2001||05:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>I just ordered a Spintech muffler... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>COOL!  I'm wanting to get the complete West Coast Fiero exhaust: Hi Flo cat, Spin Tech muffler, and 2.5" exhaust piping.  It's a bit out of budget right now, so Brian's hooking me up with the exhaust off of his parts car.  That should keep my beast a bit quieter 'till I can redo everything from scratch.  I'm looking forward to hearing how it sounds.  The sound clips on the website don't really tell you much.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Capt Fiero||08-07-2001||05:36 PM||||Are you guys aware that the Camaro uses a single inlet dual outlet muffler on there V6 cars. It is a bit longer than the Fiero muffler but that is not a problem for most exhaust shops.  Also the 3 prong hangers need to be either transferd to your muffler or a new set bent up and installed.  Also if you are looking for the ultimate in high flow growl systems.  Fiero Conversions in windsor ontario canada sells a complete exhaust system that does not even use a muffler, just 4 monza style resonators.  It does not include a cat so you will have to look into that further.||||reg||1
